---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../components/Byline.astro";
import DualDoors from "../components/DualDoors.astro";
import LegalNote from "../components/LegalNote.astro";
import { FROZEN } from "../lib/frozen";
import { CANON_PATHS } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const path = "/sell-through-vs-search-intent";
const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "What sold vs what they asked", path },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What sold is not what people asked for | FFL Intel"
  description="A gun that rang is real. A search that came back empty is also real. Only one of those shows up in the monthly Index. Betsy BI is the other number."
  path={path}
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.search}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-800 mb-3">
      Betsy BI
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink text-balance mb-4">
      What sold is not what people asked for
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-700 mb-6">
      One number is what rang. The other is what they tried to find. Mixing
      them is how a Monday meeting goes wrong.
    </p>
    <Byline dateLabel="August 13, 2026" read="5 min" />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-stone-200">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.search)}
        alt="A shopper searching a phone in front of an empty case"
        width="1792"
        height="1008"
        class="w-full object-cover object-top max-h-80"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-stone-700 font-serif">
      <p>{FROZEN.doctrine}</p>
      <p>
        A gun that sold at the same stores is real. A search that came back
        empty is also real. Only one of those is in Gearfire’s monthly number.
        March, minus 11.9 percent, Outdoor Wire, 13 April. We will not invent
        a Betsy Live percentage and set it next to that number as if it were
        their Index. Last month’s sales cannot see what people asked for.
        That is the whole point.
      </p>
      <p>
        Last month’s sales report is last season’s map. Useful. Late. The
        missing piece is the sentence someone typed when nothing on the shelf
        answered back. An empty search never becomes a unit sold. It still
        happened.
      </p>
      <p>
        Betsy BI is that third number — GunSearchEngine, dealer-site
        GunSearchAgent, Betsy Live as a labeled sample. Not a rival monthly.
        {FROZEN.betsy}
      </p>
      <p>
        The cards below send you to the right next page. This one is just
        the explanation.
      </p>
    </div>
    <DualDoors />
    <p class="mt-10"><LegalNote /></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
